Since the model relies on Query, Key, and Value matrices that come from the same source (i.e., the input sequence or context window), this eliminates the need for RNNs, completely ensuring parallelizability for the architecture. This differs from the original form of the Attention mechanism introduced in 2014. Additionally, the paper discusses the use of an additional scaling factor that was found to be most effective with respect to the dimension of the key vectors (represented as dk and initially set to 64 within the paper) in the manner shown above.
